{"post": true, "caption": "A coin's price alone tells you almost nothing. Its total value is price x number of coins. That's called market cap.\nIn this example, for Coin A to reach $1, its total value would have to grow 100x, to $100 billion.\nBefore you call a coin cheap, check how many coins exist.\nDid you know this? Yes or no.\n\nEducation only. Not financial advice.\n\n#CandleAndCode #TradingForBeginners #CryptoBasics #MarketCap", "tag": "MYTH VS REALITY", "footer": "Education only. Not financial advice.", "bpm": 100, "scenes": [{"type": "hook", "dur": 2.4, "size": 130, "lines": [{"t": "$0.01 COIN.", "c": "green"}, {"t": "NOT CHEAP.", "c": "red"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 2.8, "size": 88, "lines": [{"t": "Low price = cheap?", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Here's the catch.", "c": "muted"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "size": 88, "lines": [{"t": "Price alone means", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "almost nothing.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Count the coins.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "stat", "dur": 3.0, "label": "Coin A: $0.01 x 100 billion coins", "value": "$1B", "note": "Total value of all coins.", "c": "green"}, {"type": "stat", "dur": 3.0, "label": "Coin B: $50 x 2 million coins", "value": "$100M", "note": "Pricier coin. 10x smaller.", "c": "green"}, {"type": "bars", "dur": 5.0, "title": "Which one is bigger?", "subtitle": "total value, two made-up coins", "rows": [{"l": "Coin A, $0.01", "v": 1000, "vl": "$1B", "lc": "fg", "bc": "green"}, {"l": "Coin B, $50", "v": 100, "vl": "$100M", "lc": "fg", "bc": "red"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.2, "size": 84, "lines": [{"t": "Stop asking", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "how cheap it is.", "c": "red"}, {"t": "Ask how big it is.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "end", "dur": 2.2, "line": "Trade with a system, not a feeling."}]}